.html\n│   login.html\n│   register.html\n│\n├─admin/\n│   (empty for now – will host admin pages later)\n│\n├─seller/\n│   (empty for now – will host seller pages later)\n│\n├─customer/\n│   cart.html\n│   (other customer pages to be added later)\n│\n├─assets/\n│   ├─css/\n│   │   style.css\n│   ├─js/\n│   │   storage.js\n│   │   auth.js\n│   │   main.js\n│   │   products.js\n│   │   product-details.js\n│   │   cart.js\n│   └─images/\n│       (placeholder images can be added)\n```\n\n### 🎯 Next steps (choose which to continue)\n\n| Phase | Goal |\n|------|------|\n| **1 – Home page polish** | Populate more sample categories/products, improve hero banner, add “Featured” & “Latest” sections. |\n| **2 – Customer dashboard & orders** | `customer/dashboard.html`, order history (`orders.html`), order details, checkout flow, payment simulation. |\n| **3 – Seller workflow** | `seller/dashboard.html`, add/edit/delete product forms, pending‑approval view, order list with status updates, simple sales report. |\n| **4 – Admin workflow** | `admin/dashboard.html`, user management, category CRUD, product‑approval page, order overview, basic reports. |\n| **5 – Reviews & ratings** | Allow customers to submit a review after delivery, display on product‑details page. |\n| **6 – Final polish & deployment** | Add missing pages, improve responsiveness, test on desktop/mobile, push to GitHub, enable GitHub Pages, verify all links work.\n\nLet me know which phase you’d like to start with, or if you need any adjustments before proceeding."}
{"step_index":46,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:21:45Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nContinue the E-Commerce Shopping Website project with **Phase 2 – Customer Dashboard & Orders**.\n\nFirst inspect the existing project files. Reuse the existing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. Do not recreate working features or change the existing design unnecessarily.\n\n### 1. Create customer pages\n\nInside the existing `customer/` folder, create:\n\n- `dashboard.html`\n- `checkout.html`\n- `orders.html`\n- `profile.html`\n\nThe existing `cart.html` must continue working.\n\n### 2. Customer Dashboard\n\nCreate a simple dashboard displaying:\n- Welcome message with the logged-in customer's name.\n- Total orders.\n- Pending orders.\n- Recently placed orders.\n- Quick links to Products, Cart, My Orders, and Profile.\n\n### 3. Checkout\n\nImplement a basic checkout page.\n\nDisplay:\n- Products being ordered.\n- Quantity.\n- Individual product price.\n- Total amount.\n- Customer name and delivery address.\n- Payment method selection.\n\nPayment methods:\n- UPI (simulation only).\n- Card (simulation only; do not collect real card details).\n- Cash on Delivery.\n\nAdd a Place Order button.\n\n### 4. Order Processing\n\nWhen the customer places an order:\n\n1. Validate the shopping cart.\n2. Check available product stock.\n3. Prevent ordering more than the available quantity.\n4. Calculate the final total.\n5. Save the order in LocalStorage.\n6. Reduce the available product stock.\n7. Clear the customer's cart.\n8. Display an order confirmation message.\n9. Make the order available to the relevant seller and administrator through shared LocalStorage data in the same browser.\n\nInitial order status: `Placed`.\n\n### 5. My Orders\n\nCreate a simple order history page showing:\n- Order ID.\n- Order date.\n- Products.\n- Total amount.\n- Payment method.\n- Payment status.\n- Order status.\n\nAllow customers to view their order details.\n\n### 6. Profile\n\nDisplay the logged-in customer's basic information:\n- Name.\n- Email.\n- Phone number, if available.\n- Delivery address.\n\nAllow basic profile editing.\n\n### 7. Important coding instructions\n\n- Use only HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript.\n- Reuse the existing `storage.js`, `auth.js`, and `main.js`.\n- Keep the existing blue-and-white design.\n- Use beginner-friendly JavaScript.\n- Use LocalStorage for data.\n- Ensure relative paths work from the `customer/` folder.\n- Do not add advanced features or unnecessary libraries.\n- Do not break existing login, registration, product listing, or cart functionality.\n\n### 8. Testing\n\nTest the complete customer workflow:\n\nLogin → Browse Products → Add to Cart → Checkout → Place Order → View My Orders.\n\nAlso test insufficient stock, empty cart, and invalid checkout details.\n\nAfter completing Phase 2:\n- List all files created or modified.\n- Report which features work.\n- Report any remaining issues.\n- Stop and wait for my approval before starting Phase 3 – Seller Workflow.\n\nKeep everything basic and suitable for a beginner-level college project.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-17T09:51:45+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
