{"step_index":51,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:21:57Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":31923,"cache_read_tokens":3839,"output_tokens":876,"thinking":"We need to create orders.html, profile.html, also JavaScript files: dashboard.js, checkout.js, orders.js, profile.js.\n\nImplement simple JS functionality.\n\nWe must ensure relative paths and usage of existing storage.\n\nImplement dashboard.js to fetch session, orders, display totals, recent.\n\ncheckout.js to render cart items, handle form submit, validate stock, create order, update storage.\n\norders.js to display list of orders for current customer, with details.\n\nprofile.js to display and edit profile info; stored in user data.\n\nAlso need to add cart link short but currently cart.html path is relative to customer folder: ../customer/cart.html? Actually cart.html is inside customer folder; from dashboard, link is cart.html (same folder). Good.\n\nNow we implement each.\n\nPotential naming: assets/js folder currently holds storage, auth, main, products, product-details, cart. We can add new js files in same folder or create inside customer folder? Path requested: \"Inside the existing `customer/` folder, create: dashboard.html, checkout.html, orders.html, profile.html\". JS files can be placed in assets/js but referenced from pages. We'll put them in `assets/js/` as new files: `dashboard.js`, `checkout.js`, `orders.js`, `profile.js`.\n\nImplement simple code.\n\nNeed to ensure storage keys for orders have an array.\n\nWe'll store order object structure:\n\n{\n orderId: 'ORD-<timestamp>-<rand>',\n customerId: sess.userId,\n items: [{productId, quantity, price}], // capture price at time\n total: number,\n paymentMethod,\n paymentStatus: 'paid' (for UPI/Card) or 'pending' for COD,\n deliveryStatus: 'Placed',\n deliveryInfo: {fullName, address, phone},\n orderDate: new Date().toISOString()\n}\n\nWhen order placed, reduce product stock (update product array) and set status to out_of_stock if stock becomes 0.\n\nAlso need to clear cart for this user.\n\nWe'll also add order to storage.\n\nNow implement dashboard.js.\n\nProceed to write files.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// dashboard.js – customer dashboard logic\\n(function(){\\n    const storage = window.StorageAPI;\\n    const sess = storage.getSession();\\n    if(!sess || sess.role!=='customer'){\\n        alert('Please log in as a customer');\\n        window.location.href='../login.html';\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    // Populate welcome name\\n    document.getElementById('custName').textContent = sess.name || sess.email;\\n\\n    const orders = storage.get(storage.keys.orders) || [];\\n    const myOrders = orders.filter(o=>o.customerId===sess.userId);\\n    // totals\\n    document.getElementById('totalOrders').textContent = myOrders.length;\\n    const pending = myOrders.filter(o=>o.deliveryStatus==='Placed' || o.deliveryStatus==='Packed' || o.deliveryStatus==='Shipped');\\n    document.getElementById('pendingOrders').textContent = pending.length;\\n\\n    // recent orders (most recent 3)\\n    const recentContainer = document.getElementById('recentOrders');\\n    const recent = myOrders.slice(-3).reverse(); // latest first\\n    if(recent.length===0){\\n        recentContainer.innerHTML = '<p>No recent orders.</p>';\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    recent.forEach(order=>{\\n        const div = document.createElement('div');\\n        div.className='card';\\n        div.innerHTML = `\\n            <p><strong>Order ID:</strong> ${order.orderId}</p>\\n            <p><strong>Date:</strong> ${new Date(order.orderDate).toLocaleString()}</p>\\n            <p><strong>Total:</strong> ₹${order.total.toFixed(2)}</p>\\n            <p><strong>Status:</strong> ${order.deliveryStatus}</p>\\n            <a href=\\\"orders.html\\\" class=\\\"btn\\\">View All Orders</a>\\n        `;\\n        recentContainer.appendChild(div);\\n    });\\n})();\""}}]}
