{"step_index":79,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:24:10Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":41599,"cache_read_tokens":3839,"output_tokens":903,"thinking":"We need to implement JavaScript for these seller pages: dashboard.js, add-product.js, manage-products.js, manage-orders.js, reports.js.\n\nAlso need to ensure the navigation works with main.js existing.\n\nNeed to check existing files for any needed dependencies.\n\nLet's open storage.js, auth.js, main.js to ensure functions like getSession etc. Already used.\n\nOpen storage.js snippet from earlier. Already includes keys, seed, etc.\n\nWe need to add in seller dashboard the counts.\n\nAdd seller dashboard script.\n\nAdd add-product script to handle form, populate categories, save product with pending status.\n\nManage-products script to list seller's products, allow edit, delete, view status and rejection remarks.\n\nWe need edit product page? Not requested. Could allow inline editing; but simple edit form can be in same page via a modal or simple prompt.\n\nGiven beginner level, we can allow editing via a form that appears when clicking Edit; using prompt.\n\nImplement manage-products.js:\n\n- fetch seller session, get products where sellerId matches.\n\n- render each as card with name, price, stock, status, edit/delete buttons.\n\n- Edit: prompt for fields (maybe name, price, stock, description, image, category). For simplicity, we can show a simple prompt for each field.\n\n- Delete: confirm then remove from storage.\n\n- Show rejection remarks if status is 'rejected'.\n\nManage-orders.js:\n\n- fetch orders where any item.sellerId matches logged-in seller.\n\n- Show orderId, customer name (need to fetch user), product name, quantity, date, status (deliveryStatus). Provide a select dropdown to update status: Placed, Packed, Shipped, Delivered. Only allow progression forward.\n\n- On change, update order.deliveryStatus and persist.\n\nReports.js:\n\n- Simple placeholder: calculate total revenue for seller: sum of order items where sellerId matches and status delivered? maybe all. Show count orders, total revenue.\n\nImplement seller/dashboard.js:\n\n- similar to customer dashboard but seller-specific.\n\nLet's implement these.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// dashboard.js – seller dashboard logic\\n(function(){\\n    const storage = window.StorageAPI;\\n    const sess = storage.getSession();\\n    if(!sess || sess.role!=='seller'){\\n        alert('Please log in as a seller');\\n        window.location.href='../login.html';\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    // welcome name\\n    document.getElementById('sellerName').textContent = sess.name || sess.email;\\n\\n    const products = storage.get(storage.keys.products) || [];\\n    const myProducts = products.filter(p=>p.sellerId===sess.userId);\\n    const total = myProducts.length;\\n    const approved = myProducts.filter(p=>p.status==='approved').length;\\n    const pending = myProducts.filter(p=>p.status==='pending').length;\\n\\n    document.getElementById('totalProducts').textContent = total;\\n    document.getElementById('approvedProducts').textContent = approved;\\n    document.getElementById('pendingProducts').textContent = pending;\\n\\n    // orders for seller\\n    const orders = storage.get(storage.keys.orders) || [];\\n    const sellerOrders = orders.filter(o=>o.items.some(it=>it.sellerId===sess.userId));\\n    document.getElementById('totalOrders').textContent = sellerOrders.length;\\n\\n    // recent 3 orders\\n    const recentContainer = document.getElementById('recentOrders');\\n    const recent = sellerOrders.slice(-3).reverse();\\n    if(recent.length===0){\\n        recentContainer.innerHTML = '<p>No recent orders.</p>';\\n    } else {\\n        recent.forEach(order=>{\\n            const div = document.createElement('div');\\n            div.className='card';\\n            div.innerHTML = `\\n                <p><strong>Order ID:</strong> ${order.orderId}</p>\\n                <p><strong>Date:</strong> ${new Date(order.orderDate).toLocaleString()}</p>\\n                <p><strong>Status:</strong> ${order.deliveryStatus}</p>\\n            `;\\n            recentContainer.appendChild(div);\\n        });\\n    }\\n})();\""}}]}
